  "note": "Repeated queries on the same unchanged full measured-source TIN; not independent surveys or accuracy ground truth. No transformed/generated coordinates or extra thinning. Native PLY order differs from browser LOD order. An independent preceding archived production oracle exits before current native contexts start. Fresh and retained modes use the same frozen native executable in separate contexts; only one computes at a time. Retained construction moves original mesh vectors into PreparedMesh without cloning/reordering/coordinate conversion, validates faces once and builds the existing copied-corner BVH in the fixed pool. Preparation time and logical capacity bytes are recorded separately. Retained query calls borrow immutable storage and use the shared native parallel query policy; fresh calls build/drop BVHs inside each call. Both retain original serial Morton preparation/sorting, 4096-point chunks, chunk-local warm states, copied corners, clamped sibling SIMD, scalar triangle projection, compact f64 results and serial scatter. Query order and scratch are rebuilt each call; no cross-query cache or global retention is added. Retained ownership releases geometry/BVH when the object is dropped. Hot whole-call timing includes pool installation, Morton work, parallel queries, result allocation/scatter and call-local destruction; fresh additionally includes BVH build/destruction. Constructor time and final retained-object destruction are outside hot clocks. Source geometry remains owned in both contexts. Logical retained bytes include mesh and BVH vector capacities, exclude headers/allocator/pages, and do not establish process RSS or net peak memory reduction. Loading, meshing, pool creation, first observations, five warmups, serialization/statistics/parity and cleanup are excluded. All ten alternating timed pairs and outliers are retained. Setup amortization is an estimate from one observed constructor cost divided by median paired hot-call savings, excludes